<section id="theory">

<div class="section-header">

    <div class="section-number">
        MODULE 01
    </div>

    <h2>
        Information is not the same thing as understanding.
    </h2>

    <p class="lead">

        A learner can memorize hundreds of facts and still be unable
        to diagnose a complex problem. Higher-order education changes
        the task from reproducing information to constructing,
        testing and revising explanations.

    </p>

</div>


<div class="theory">

    <div class="theory-card">

        <h3>
            Lower-order learning
        </h3>

        <p>

            The learner receives information, stores it and reproduces
            it when prompted.

        </p>

        <div class="quote">

            "What is this?"

        </div>

        <p style="margin-top:20px;">

            This is useful for establishing foundations, terminology
            and basic factual knowledge.

        </p>

    </div>


    <div class="theory-card highlight">

        <h3>
            Analytical learning
        </h3>

        <p>

            The learner examines conditions, compares competing
            explanations, evaluates evidence, predicts consequences
            and designs an intervention.

        </p>

        <div class="quote">

            "Why is this happening, what else could explain it,
            and what would happen if we changed the system?"

        </div>

    </div>

</div>


